    "result_text": "Done. The change is implemented and the full test suite is green.\n\n## What I did\n\nThe spec required emitting an audit line via the logger named `AUDIT` on successful owner create, carrying the owner id, `customerCode` and `registrationDate`.\n\n**1. New audit function step** \u2014 `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java`:\n\n```java\npublic class AuditOwnerCreated {\n    private static final Logger AUDIT = LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\");\n\n    public void service(@Val Owner owner) {\n        AUDIT.info(\"Owner created id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={}\",\n                owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate());\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**2. Wired it into the create pipeline** \u2014 `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`, inserting an `audit` step between `save` and `respond`:\n\n```yaml\nsave:\n  ...\n  next: audit\n\naudit:\n  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.AuditOwnerCreated\n  govern: [ transaction ]\n  next: respond\n```\n\n## Why this shape\n\n- The step runs **after `SaveOwner`**, so `owner.getId()` is assigned by then; before `respond`, so it can't affect the HTTP response. It follows the project's OfficeFloor function-injection convention (one public method, `@Val Owner` reads the shared entity) rather than a Spring controller.\n- The logger is created via `LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\")` \u2014 the literal SLF4J logger name the test's `AuditLogCapture` attaches its Logback appender to.\n- `registrationDate` is a `LocalDate`, whose `toString()` is ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`, matching the JSON `registrationDate` text the test compares against.\n\n## Verification\n\nThe existing acceptance test `AcceptanceTest.coreLogsAuditOnCreate` passes, and the full `./mvnw test` suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0). The emitted line is visible in the run, e.g. `AUDIT - Owner created id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-09-07`.",
